# In the drivers' component rather than main/Kconfig.projbuild, so that the
# firmware and the on-target test app (apps/firmware_esp32/test_app/), which
# link this component but not main/, see the same symbol.

menu "Home Air Monitor: sensor drivers"

    config HAC_BSEC
        bool "Compute IAQ with Bosch's BSEC2 (needs its library in third_party/bsec/)"
        default n
        help
            Phase 3d (docs/adr/0020-bsec-iaq.md). Measures the BME68x through
            drivers/bme68x/bme68x_bsec_source.c: Bosch's BSEC2 library decides
            when the sensor measures and with which heater profile, compensates
            temperature and humidity for the sensor's own heating, and computes
            an index of air quality, which the home screen shows in its IAQ
            cell. BSEC's CO2 equivalent is never computed.

            Needs Bosch's BSEC2 2.6.1.0 archive, downloaded after accepting
            Bosch's licence agreement and unpacked as it comes into
            third_party/bsec/, which is gitignored (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
            It is never committed, so this is off by default: CI and a fresh
            clone build without it, and the BME68x is then measured by
            drivers/bme68x/bme68x_source.c and the IAQ cell shows raw gas
            resistance (docs/requirements.md 17.2).

            Build it in a directory and sdkconfig of its own, from
            sdkconfig.bsec, so the setting never depends on an sdkconfig made
            before the symbol existed:

              idf.py -B build-bsec -D SDKCONFIG=build-bsec/sdkconfig \
                  -D "SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS=sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.bsec" build

            An image built with this carries Bosch's proprietary library: do
            not attach it to a release (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

endmenu
